{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790470765,"nonce":"FyL6I1RU6Y4OjGCfH6PWilmxmTM=","title":"Python: += on a boxed list of one kind by another kind rebinds when the list was not made for a dynamic name","message":"d2e25071 builds a list literal, comprehension, slice, concatenation, list() or sorted() as a list of dynamic values when it is bound to a dynamic name, passed to a dynamic parameter, or returned from a function returning a dynamic value, so += and extend of any kind grow it in place. A list that reaches a dynamic slot any other way is still boxed at its own kind, and zb_any_arith_inplace grows it in place only by values of that kind; otherwise the name is rebound to a new list and an alias keeps the old one:\n\n    def g(v):\n        w = v\n        v += [None]\n        return w\n    print(g(\"ab\" if n \u003e 100 else [7]))   # CPython [7, None]; zypy [7]\n\nThe same holds for extend and insert through a dynamic receiver of such a list (TypeError for a kind that does not convert). Growing the boxed list in place needs either the box to be retargeted at a widened list (every dynamic alias holds the same box) or the storage converted in place, and neither is sound while a typed alias of the same list may exist; 202606d's unification is the general fix.","files":null}]}